<h2>cat research_interests.md</h2>

<p class="research-thesis reveal">
  My research looks at how foundation models perceive, represent and reason about the physical 3D and 4D world. I diagnose where current multimodal systems fall back on linguistic shortcuts, and build grounded representations that transfer to embodied agents.
</p>

<div class="interests-grid">
  <div class="interest-card reveal" style="--accent: var(--primary-color);">
    <span class="interest-code">01 // SPATIAL &amp; 4D</span>
    <strong>Spatial &amp; 4D Reasoning</strong>
    <span class="interest-desc">Why do multimodal models fail to perceive geometry, motion, and physical space—and how do we fix it?</span>
  </div>
  <div class="interest-card reveal" style="--accent: var(--heading-color);">
    <span class="interest-code">02 // MULTIMODAL</span>
    <strong>Grounded Multimodal Models</strong>
    <span class="interest-desc">How can we align vision, language, and generative models with real-world structure instead of surface shortcuts?</span>
  </div>
  <div class="interest-card reveal" style="--accent: #a78bfa;">
    <span class="interest-code">03 // WORLD MODELING</span>
    <strong>Representation &amp; World Modeling</strong>
    <span class="interest-desc">How can models learn structured, generalizable representations of dynamic environments without heavy supervision?</span>
  </div>
  <div class="interest-card reveal" style="--accent: var(--primary-color);">
    <span class="interest-code">04 // EMBODIED</span>
    <strong>Embodied AI &amp; Robotics</strong>
    <span class="interest-desc">How do we turn 3D/4D perception and spatiotemporal reasoning into physical action and human-robot collaboration?</span>
  </div>
</div>

